WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.480
A battle between interdimensional entities and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.800
giving birth to a bouncing bundle of&nbsp;
terror! Get ready to dig into all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.720
gory details surrounding the ending of&nbsp;
"Terrifier 2." Beware! Spoilers ahead!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.680
The "Miles County Massacre" is the&nbsp;
name given to the events of the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.700
"Terrifier" movie in the universe&nbsp;
of "Terrifier 2." There are frequent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.720
references to this event throughout&nbsp;
the sequel, which takes place exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.100
one year after that event as Jonathan has&nbsp;
developed an obsession with the killings.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.840
"You think that guy's still out there?"

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.540
"What's up with you and this clown all&nbsp;
of a sudden? You're, like, obsessed."

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.920
"They never found his body."

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.560
But it's not just Jonathan — there's a broader&nbsp;
cultural interest in the events as well. A talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.540
show host interviews the sole survivor of the&nbsp;
original bloodbath, Victoria Heyes. And there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:51.720
significant news coverage of the event marking its&nbsp;
anniversary on TV, online, and in the newspapers.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.720
"Terrifier 2" largely stands&nbsp;
on its own narratively,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.260
and viewers don't need to have seen the&nbsp;
first film to understand what the "Miles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.040
County Massacre" was. It also helps&nbsp;
that the attention paid to the "Miles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.080
County Massacre" in "Terrifier 2" is ultimately&nbsp;
more thematically important than narratively.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:14.700
"Please, welcome…Art&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:15.476
the Clown!"

00:01:15.476 --> 00:01:20.820
Art the Clown made his first appearance in Damien&nbsp;
Leone's 2011 short film "Terrifier," where the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:25.740
character was played by Mike Gianelli. That short&nbsp;
then became a segment in Leone's first feature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.480
the anthology movie "All Hallow's Eve." But&nbsp;
already in "All Hallow's Eve" it seems that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.620
Art isn't just a man dressed in clown&nbsp;
makeup as he makes his entrance via a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.720
TV set as the characters watch an evil VHS&nbsp;
tape. David Howard Thornton took over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.520
role when Art took the spotlight for 2013's&nbsp;
"Terrifier," which ends with Art seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.900
dead from a self-inflicted gunshot wound&nbsp;
before his body disappears from a morgue.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.560
"Terrifier 2" pushes things even&nbsp;
further as it reintroduces Art,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.540
who still has a gaping head wound, but is&nbsp;
otherwise fine. There's no real explanation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.520
given for how the clown survived, but as the&nbsp;
sequel goes on, we get some hints. It seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.660
that Art may be a cosmic or supernatural&nbsp;
entity in the same way that some fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:11.040
believe Michael Myers from "Halloween" is&nbsp;
simply the embodiment of metaphysical evil.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.700
As we learn more about Sienna's&nbsp;
father's visions in "Terrifier 2,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.480
there's some evidence that Art is far&nbsp;
more than a human in a clown outfit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.220
and is instead something mythical. That would&nbsp;
explain why he can pass into reality through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:28.380
media and why he seems to be unkillable, but&nbsp;
it doesn't quite explain his particular glee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.700
in the horrific violence he commits —&nbsp;
that remains disturbingly inexplicable.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.260
Sienna is a high schooler struggling with&nbsp;
the recent loss of her father to suicide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:42.240
while attempting to maintain good relationships&nbsp;
with her brother Jonathan and their mom Barbara.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.320
When we meet her, she's making a Halloween&nbsp;
costume based on the fantasy character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:51.000
that her dad - an artist - created for her.&nbsp;
Along with creating the fantasy character for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.860
Sienna, her dad also gave her a sword that&nbsp;
seems to hold mystical powers and is one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:00.660
the only weapons that can defend against Art's&nbsp;
evil and cause significant damage to the clown.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.400
From everything we can see she's just a regular&nbsp;
teenager living through the ups and downs of life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:10.260
But in a dream sequence early in "Terrifier 2,"&nbsp;
we can see that there's something special about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:15.480
her when her dream has an effect on reality&nbsp;
and starts a fire. As the movie goes on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.380
Sienna becomes Art's target while&nbsp;
Jonathan furthers his investigations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:24.360
into the connection their father had to Art,&nbsp;
and eventually, he theorizes that Sienna is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:29.100
the only one who can truly defeat the clown.&nbsp;
Her importance only becomes clearer when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.240
confronts Art at the end of the movie and&nbsp;
even manages to come back from the dead.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.280
We can't say for sure whether Sienna is the same&nbsp;
kind of cosmic or supernatural entity as Art,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:43.080
or whether she is simply capable of channeling&nbsp;
the timeless being that her father discovered and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.400
said he created for her. Either way, we can&nbsp;
say for sure that she's a great final girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.980
and there's certainly something magical about her.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:55.740
"Terrifier 2" introduces audiences to a character&nbsp;
that's never named but credited as "The Little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.740 --> 00:04:00.660
Pale Girl." Early on in the film, when Art visits&nbsp;
a laundromat to clean up after murdering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:05.760
unlucky coroner who was to inspect his body, the&nbsp;
girl appears in the laundromat and shoots him a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.100
wide, creepy clown smile. She then approaches Art&nbsp;
and engages him in a silent game of patty cake.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:16.080
It's a bizarre moment that raises a lot of&nbsp;
questions — one of which is quickly answered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.760
at least partially. We get to see that from&nbsp;
the point of view of the only other person in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.780
the laundromat, Art is playing patty cake&nbsp;
with the air. So it seems that The Little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.760
Pale Girl may simply be a vision of Art's,&nbsp;
but Sienna and her brother Jonathan can see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.380
her as well. The reason Sienna and Jonathan&nbsp;
can see her and others can't is undoubtedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:38.460
due to the strange link that they have with Art&nbsp;
that we'll talk about a little more in a moment.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.740
After first seeing The Little Pale Girl, Jonathan&nbsp;
does some research and discovers that she looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.840
exactly like a girl who is believed to have been&nbsp;
Art's first victim. It's possible then that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:54.060
girl's soul has somehow been transformed and bound&nbsp;
to Art in a way that has made her his attendant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.500
allowing her to keep him company as he&nbsp;
terrorizes people. But she isn't simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.000
a passive observer. Instead, she takes an&nbsp;
active role in Art's nefarious schemes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.260
as we see when she mimics Jonathan's&nbsp;
voice in a call to Sienna. Albeit she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.780
seems to suspect something isn't&nbsp;
quite right about the phone call.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:15.840
"I know when Jonathan's lying okay? I…I could hear&nbsp;
it in his voice. Something's, Something's wrong."

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.400
Giving us reason to ponder what her&nbsp;
possible supernatural abilities might be.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.960
While we can't say for certain what the&nbsp;
connection is between Art and Sienna,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.280
we have some ideas. At first, when Jonathan&nbsp;
shows Sienna that their dad had drawn Art&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.540
and was collecting newspaper clippings about&nbsp;
his killings, it seems possible that perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:38.880
their father is Art. Either he faked his death&nbsp;
to become this deranged killer, or he somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.920
became the host of a metaphysical evil and hasn't&nbsp;
entirely lost his connection to his human life.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.360
But as the movie goes on, the former&nbsp;
seems impossible given what we learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.440
about his death. The latter, though, seems&nbsp;
like it may still be true, and that leads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:56.640
to our two theories about what exactly the&nbsp;
connection may be. The first is that her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.680
father's tumor caused him to see beyond human&nbsp;
reality and see two warring eternal entities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:06.900
one evil and one good, this would then allow&nbsp;
for the possibility that the evil entity has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:11.340
somehow taken over her father's essence. The&nbsp;
other is that her dad somehow brought Art to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:16.020
life from his own psyche through the power of&nbsp;
his, well, art. This would also explain why he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.400
was able to create a character for his daughter&nbsp;
and a weapon that can stand against the clown.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:25.260
Sienna's dream sequence near the start of&nbsp;
"Terrifier 2" may be one of the longest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:30.240
dream sequences in any horror movie. She&nbsp;
dreams of a strange children's TV show set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.640
where a woman sings a jaunty song about a clown&nbsp;
café, young people hang out on a small playset,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:40.200
and a line of adults is queued up at a food&nbsp;
truck — a food truck with Art's face on it.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:44.700
Nearby a young boy is filming a cereal&nbsp;
commercial for an Art-themed cereal that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:49.200
includes roaches and razor blades. We see&nbsp;
the boy chew some of the disgusting cereal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.280
and bleed from the mouth before reaching&nbsp;
into the box for a surprise. Suddenly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:58.560
Art appears and kills everyone on set. He uses&nbsp;
increasingly wild weapons like a big machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.520
gun and a flame thrower to devastate&nbsp;
the sets and all the people on them.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:06.720
It seems like it's just a horrifying&nbsp;
dream, but when Sienna deflects the fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:11.100
from Art's flame thrower with her father's&nbsp;
sword, she causes a real fire to appear in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:15.180
her bedroom. And later in the movie when&nbsp;
she's stabbed by Art with the same sword,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.420
she falls into a tank of water on&nbsp;
the set that she saw in her dream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:23.700
but now everyone is dead and mutilated. We can't&nbsp;
be sure whether Sienna's dream was a glimpse of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:27.300
something that happened in the real world,&nbsp;
but it was certainly more than just a dream.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:32.280
After Art stabs Sienna with the sword her&nbsp;
father gave her, she falls through a hole in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.720
the Terrifier ride at the carnival where Art has&nbsp;
lured her. But she doesn't just fall into dirt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:41.400
or another level of concrete — she falls into&nbsp;
a water tank on the edge of the scene from her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:45.780
dream. More than being confined to a water tank&nbsp;
that's drowning her, she's also being held down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:50.700
by something that looks equally like a frayed&nbsp;
rope, a worm, and a decomposing human hand.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:54.420
Again, it seems possible that this is&nbsp;
her seeing something of Art's world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:58.800
that he has transported her here by killing&nbsp;
her with the mystical weapon bestowed upon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:04.020
her by her father. But she refuses to accept&nbsp;
defeat. She struggles to get loose and while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.520
she isn't able to succeed at first, she is&nbsp;
finally able to break free and heal herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:12.540
through what seems to be a sheer force of&nbsp;
will motivated by her love for her brother.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.900
She thinks of Jonathan and how she&nbsp;
wants to keep him safe from Art,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:20.280
and the sword begins to glow along with her&nbsp;
stomach wound. The wound then begins to heal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:24.720
and she can break free of whatever is holding&nbsp;
her in the tank before returning to the land of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:29.640
the living and decapitating Art. To say that the&nbsp;
power of love brought her back may sound cheesy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:34.260
but it also seems true. She was unwilling to&nbsp;
allow her brother to die horribly at the hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:38.940
of the sadistic clown, and that power allowed&nbsp;
her to will herself back to life as we know it.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:44.700
While the first "Terrifier" clocks in under 90&nbsp;
minutes and overwhelmingly focuses on delivering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:49.620
extremely disturbing horror sequences for the&nbsp;
duration of its runtime, "Terrifier 2" is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:54.960
heftier film at a full 2 hours and 18 minutes. And&nbsp;
while some might have been interested in a pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:00.060
slasher that lasts that long, Leone has packed&nbsp;
this sequel full of subtler thematic exploration.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:05.880
First and foremost are the themes of grief,&nbsp;
trauma, and mental illness as Sienna, Jonathan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:09.780
and Barbara are all still reeling from the&nbsp;
death of their beloved father and husband.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.920
The movie spends time with them as they talk&nbsp;
about their loss and the different ways that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.540
they have responded to it, and whether those&nbsp;
coping mechanisms are healthy. But the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:24.000
is also interested in how the media fixates on&nbsp;
and often exploits real-life tragedies. There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.680
significant time spent showing different kinds&nbsp;
of news coverage of Art's murders, and especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:33.540
the attention paid to how poorly Victoria is&nbsp;
treated by the talk show host after her interview.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.140
"Yeah, well, if you think she&nbsp;
looks that bad on television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:41.460
imagine what she looks like sitting two feet away&nbsp;
from you. Thought I was gonna gag at one point."

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:47.640
Most abstractly, but perhaps most fascinatingly,&nbsp;
"Terrifier 2" seems to be asking questions about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.900
horror movies and what we want from them.&nbsp;
Art is constantly mugging for the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:56.460
waving his hands, smiling, and laughing&nbsp;
at the horrific violence he enacts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:00.360
essentially inviting the audience&nbsp;
to enjoy his cruelty with him. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:04.620
the violence in the movie is so intense&nbsp;
and so realistically rendered that it'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:09.060
likely be impossible for most viewers to&nbsp;
experience these as fun kills in a slasher.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:15.780
"Are you not entertained?!&nbsp;
Are…you…not entertained?!"

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:19.860
The mid-credits scene of "Terrifier 2"&nbsp;
doesn't involve Sienna or her family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:25.500
and instead re-centers on Victoria Heyes, who&nbsp;
has been confined to a mental hospital after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:29.940
she attacked the talk show host who insulted&nbsp;
her. At first, we only see two members of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:34.500
staff at the hospital talking about her and&nbsp;
how she's been remarkably calm as a patient.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.440
But soon we hear Victoria screaming and we see her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:41.700
writing obscenities on the wall with her&nbsp;
blood. Then her stomach starts to swell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.840
and it rapidly grows until she gives&nbsp;
birth to Art's somehow living head.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:51.240
It's a wild sequence that is nearly impossible&nbsp;
to make sense of, but our understanding is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:55.980
Victoria has become linked to Art in a similar&nbsp;
way that The Little Pale Girl has, only Victoria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.980 --> 00:11:01.500
is still living. The fact that Victoria is still&nbsp;
alive may mean that she is now Art's lifeline to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:06.840
our world. He's been defeated by Sienna and her&nbsp;
mystical sword but can return through Victoria.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:12.600
If you or anyone you know is having suicidal&nbsp;
thoughts, please call the National Suicide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:20.520
Prevention Lifeline by dialing 988&nbsp;
or by calling 1-800-273-TALK (8255)​.

